I wanted the flashback to land quietly as a private moment, not a cinematic showpiece—so S01 is a medium shot to place both men and the closed box in the same, restrained space and let the scene breathe before anything is revealed. Practically, the MS with the handheld 35mm at f/4 gives us that close-but-not-invasive feel, keeps the greenish overhead light and rain ambience readable, and leaves the top of the frame clear for the editorial title or a later cut-in; it also gives the editor an anchor to cut into tighter inserts and reactions without breaking geography. Want me to check the opening hold length—longer to sit in the mood, or tighten it to move faster into the reveal?